# Typography Philosophy

Typography is the primary communication medium of the interface.

Well-designed typography improves comprehension, reduces cognitive effort, and establishes visual hierarchy without relying on decorative elements.

Typography should always prioritize:

* Readability
* Consistency
* Clarity
* Information hierarchy
* Long-term maintainability

Text should communicate information rather than decorate the interface.

---

# Typography Principles

Every typographic decision should prioritize:

Readability

↓

Hierarchy

↓

Consistency

↓

Accessibility

↓

Brand Identity

Typography is a communication system—not decoration.

